 Let $f(x)=2x^4+11x^3-42x^2-60x+47$ and $d(x)=x^2+7x-5$. The degree of $f$ is greater than or equal to degree of $d$, so we can perform the division algorithm on $f$ and $d$. We have
\begin{align*} 2x^4+11x^3-42x^2-60x+47&=(2x^2-3)(x^2+7x-5)+(-14x+22)\\ &=(2x^2-3)d(x)-14x+22 \end{align*}
So the remainder is $-14x+22$, or $\boxed{22-14x}$. </think> <answer> 22-14x </answer>

